  "id": "DrugBank_DB00056 - MONDO_18434",
  "verbalization": "Gemtuzumab Ozogamicin is indicated for Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) with Npm1 somatic mutations, and this indication is linked to Glasdegib and Quizartinib, which are both indicated for AML with T(9;11)(p22;q23). The evidence suggests that Gemtuzumab Ozogamicin may be repurposed for AML with this specific translocation, as it shares a common indication with drugs that target similar molecular pathways. The relationship is supported by the presence of overlapping indications and the shared mechanism of action, which implies a potential overlap in therapeutic targets. The evidence also highlights the importance of Npm1 mutations in driving the disease, which may be a key factor in the repurposing of Gemtuzumab Ozogamicin for this subset of AML patients. The integration of these paths suggests that Gemtuzumab Ozogamicin could be a viable treatment option for AML with T(9;11)(p22;q23) due to its shared molecular profile with other drugs targeting similar pathologies.",
